\begin{align*}
x^2&\equiv 1\pmod{5}\implies x=\{1,4\}
x^2&\equiv 1\pmod{9}\implies x=\{1,8\}
x^2&\equiv 1\pmod{16}\implies x=\{1,7,9,15\}.
\end{align*}
By the Chinese Remainder Theorem, we see that there must be  $2\cdot 2\cdot4=\boxed{16}$  total solutions since  $0,1,2,\ldots,717,718,719$  forms a complete residue cycle.

