Now similar to the procedure we use to solve  $\sum_{i<j}f(i)f(j)$  (matrix method I guess) we make a table and find that \[\begin{aligned}\displaystyle{\prod_{i<j}V(i)V(j)}&=\frac{\sqrt{\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}}\displaystyle{\prod_{j=1}^{n}V(i)V(j)}}}{\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}}=\frac{\sqrt{\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}}\displaystyle{\prod_{j=1}^{n}V(i)}\right)\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}}\displaystyle{\prod_{j=1}^{n}V(j)}\right)}}{\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}}
&=\frac{\sqrt{\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{j=1}^{n}}\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}\right)\right)\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}}\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{j=1}^{n}V(j)}\right)\right)}}{\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}}=\frac{\sqrt{\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}\right)^n\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}\right)^n}}{\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}}
&=\frac{\sqrt{\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}\right)^{2n}}}{\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}}=\left(\displaystyle{\prod_{i=1}^{n}V(i)}\right)^{n-1}
\end{aligned}\]

Now  $\prod_{i<j} r_ir_j=\left(\prod_{i=1}^{n}r_i\right)^{10-1}=(P(0))^{9}$ And  $\prod_{i<j} (r_i-1)(r_j-1)=\prod_{i<j} (1-r_i)(1-r_j)=\left(\prod_{i=1}^{n}(1-r_i)\right)^{10-1}=(P(1))^9$  $Q(1)=2=\prod_{i<j}\frac{(r_i-1)(r_j-1)}{r_ir_j}=\frac{P(1)^9}{P(0)^9}=\frac{P(1)^9}{2^9}$  $\implies P(1)=2^{\frac{10}{9}}$  $\implies \log_2(|P(1)|)=\frac{10}{9}=\frac{m}{n}\implies m+n=\boxed{19}$

