&=\frac{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{k-1}(\frac{1}{100})(\frac{99}{100})^{2k-1}(\frac{1}{100})k}{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{k-1}(\frac{1}{100})(\frac{99}{100})^{2k-1}(\frac{1}{100})}
&=\frac{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k-2}(\frac{1}{100})^2k}{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k-2}(\frac{1}{100})^2}
&=\frac{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k}k}{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k}}
&=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^\infty\sum_{k=j}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k}}{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k}}
&=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3j}\sum_{k=0}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k}}{\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k}}
&=\sum_{k=0}^\infty(\frac{99}{100})^{3k}
&=\frac{1}{1-(\frac{99}{100})^3}
&=\frac{100^3}{100^3-99^3}.
\end{align*}

Since  $\gcd(100^3, 100^3-99^3)=\gcd(100^3, 99^3)=\gcd(100, 99)^3=1$ , the answer is 

