This third construction would not have been counted in our formula for  $p'_n$  because there is no path through  $C_n$  at all in this construction; this is a special case that only exists with  $S_1$  because there are only two vertices to be covered in  $C_1$  once  $c_1$  is removed, and they are contained in the paths through  $A_1$  and  $B_1$ . For any  $S_{n > 1}$ , there are more than two vertices to cover in  $C_n$  and a path through  $C_n$  is necessary, so the formulae above do work for  $n > 1$ .

